## What the optimiser should keep balanced
- **Mirror current ratios:** WT/WB sets the tail current, and WP/WPB sets the PMOS source current. Each PMOS source must carry more than half the tail current so the cascode branches don't starve. In other words, WP/WPB must stay above (WT/WB)/2.
- **Cascode headroom:** R1 sets the headroom of the PMOS current sources, and R2 sets the headroom of M11/M12.
- **Power:** even at the upper ranges, power should stay under 2 mW, but check total current if WT/WB and WP/WPB both go high.
